# /about was a placeholder that reached production reading "This is the
# content! This is the sidebar!". The page is gone; the URL is not, so it
# lands on the home page rather than on a 404.
/about   /   301!
/about/  /   301!

# Anything with no file behind it gets the not-found page, with a not-found
# status. Every real route is a file the build wrote, so nothing legitimate
# reaches this rule.
#
# It used to serve /index.html at 200, which meant a mistyped address answered
# with the home page and told a crawler it was a real page. With the
# documentation changing address, that would have turned every stale link into
# a duplicate of the home page.
/*  /404.html  404
